<p id="S4.T2.9" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><span id="S4.T2.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:70%;">Notes:<span id="S4.T2.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
<span id="S4.T2.9.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">ASR</span> = Attack Success Rate (%, lower is better for defender).
<span id="S4.T2.9.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">UA</span> = Utility under Attack (%, higher is better for defender).
<span id="S4.T2.9.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">LLM-Detector</span> = Qwen3Guard.
<span id="S4.T2.9.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_underline ltx_font_bold">Bold</span> indicates best result.
</span>Bold<span id="S4.T2.9.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> indicates second-best UA.
</span><span id="S4.T2.9.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ICON</span> maximizes UA with negligible impact on ASR.<span id="S4.T2.9.1.4" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p></div></div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Experiments</h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.1 </span>Experimental Setup</h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the effectiveness of <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">ICON</span> by integrating it into the ReAct <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yao et al., 2022</a>)</cite> framework, with a specific focus on the mitigation of IPI attacks. Our experiments are conducted across three representative foundation LLMs: <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Qwen</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">LLaMA</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Touvron et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, and <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Mistral</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ministral, 2025</a>)</cite>. For Visual Large Models, we utilize <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Qwen-VL</span>, <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">InternVL</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, and <span id="S5.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MiniCPM</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. These models were selected for their diverse architectures, ranging from reasoning-optimized to general-purpose designs, and their robust native support for tool-calling mechanisms.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Datasets.</span> We utilize two widely used datasets, <em id="S5.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">InjectAgent</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhan et al., 2024</a>)</cite> and <em id="S5.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">AgentDojo</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Debenedetti et al., 2024</a>)</cite> to evaluate the effectiveness of <span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">ICON</span>. For training, we adopt TrojanTools <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Anonymous, 2025</a>)</cite>, which provides diverse tool selections in order to demonstrate the out-of-distribution capability of our <span id="S5.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">ICON</span>. For visual tasks, we utilize Visual Prompt Injection Benchmarks <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wan et al., 2024</a>)</cite> provided by Meta.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Baselines.</span>
Following recent literature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bhagwatkar et al., </a>)</cite>, we benchmark <span id="S5.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter ltx_font_bold">ICON</span> against three defense mechanisms: template-based, filter-based, and fine-tuning-based.
Template-based defenses include Repeat Prompt <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Debenedetti et al., 2024</a>)</cite>, which reiterates system instructions, and Delimiting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Willison, 2023</a>)</cite>, which uses special tokens to isolate untrusted content.
For filtering-based defense, we use MELON <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhu et al., 2025</a>)</cite>, a state-of-the-art tool-filtering framework.
For fine-tuning-based defense, we utilize Qwen3Guard <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2025</a>)</cite> and Gemini <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Team et al., 2023</a>)</cite>, the most advanced (M)LLM currently available, to establish a performance upper bound for intrinsic model robustness.</p>
</div>
